**Multilingual RAG pipeline (ES/EN/FR) with multi-agent analysis over climate and energy journalism.**

Ingests 6 RSS sources → NLP enrichment → multilingual embeddings → BERTopic clustering → LLM sentiment classification → 4-agent LangGraph system → live Streamlit dashboard with SSE streaming.

[Architecture](#architecture) · [Quick Start](#quick-start) · [API Reference](#api-reference) · [Inter-System Integration](#inter-system-integration) · [Tests](#tests) · [Infrastructure](#infrastructure)

</div>

---

## Overview

The Climate & Energy Intelligence System is a project that demonstrates production-grade RAG and multi-agent architecture on a constrained (100% free-tier) infrastructure. The system continuously ingests multilingual climate and energy journalism, enriches it with NLP and LLM analysis, and exposes structured endpoints consumed by a live Streamlit dashboard and by external agent systems.

**What it does end to end:**

```
RSS Feeds (6 sources, 3 languages)
    ↓  feedparser + trafilatura
MongoDB RAW colection (300+ articles)
    ↓  spaCy (es/en/fr) + langdetect
MongoDB CLEAN colection(lemmas, NER, language)
    ↓  HF Serverless API (paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2, 384 dims)
MongoDB CLEAN colection (+embedding field)
    ↓  BERTopic (UMAP 384→5 + HDBSCAN)
MongoDB CLEAN colection (+topic_id field)
    ↓  Groq llama-3.1-8b-instant → Gemini 2.0 Flash (fallback)
MongoDB CURATED colection (sentiment, intensity, principal_subject, main_argument)
    ↓  LangGraph (Analytical → Contradiction → Trend → Synthesis)
MongoDB SUMMARIES colection (narrative summary)
    ↓  FastAPI SSE + Streamlit
Live Dashboard (4 tabs)
```

---

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        DATA LAYER — MongoDB Atlas M0                        │
│                                                                             │
│   RAW ──────► CLEAN ─────────────────────► CURATED ──────► SUMMARIES       │
│   (sha256)   (lemmas, NER, embedding,       (sentiment,     (narrative)     │
│              topic_id)                      intensity,                      │
│                                             subject, arg)                   │
└────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │ motor (async) / pymongo (sync agents)
┌────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        NLP WORKER                                           │
│                                                                             │
│  feed_reader.py ──► scraper.py ──► pipeline.py ──► embedder.py             │
│  (feedparser)       (trafilatura)  (spaCy ×3      (HF Serverless API       │
│                                    langdetect)     384-dim vectors)         │
│                                        │                                    │
│                                  topic_modeler.py ──► sentiment.py         │
│                                  (BERTopic +          (Groq → Gemini       │
│                                   UMAP + HDBSCAN)      fallback, JSON)     │
└────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │
┌────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        AGENT WORKER (LangGraph)                             │
│                                                                             │
│  analytical_agent ──► contradiction_agent ──► trend_agent ──► synthesis    │
│  (MongoDB agg by      (Atlas Vector Search    (ISO-week      (narrative     │
│   source/lang/topic)   CURATED ↔ CURATED)     regression)    → SUMMARIES)  │
└────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │ asyncio.run_in_executor
┌────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        FASTAPI  (port 8000)                                 │
│                                                                             │
│  POST /pipeline/run  (SSE streaming, 6 steps)                              │
│  GET  /health        /articles   /topics    /contradictions                 │
│       /trends        /summary    /embeddings                                │
│                                                                             │
│  ── Inter-system layer (X-RAG-Key auth) ──                                  │
│  GET  /rag/search          (Atlas Vector Search → CURATED)                  │
│  GET  /rag/topics/active   (linear regression slope, rising topics)         │
└────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │ requests (sync HTTP)
┌────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        STREAMLIT DASHBOARD (port 8501)                      │
│                                                                             │
│  Tab 1: Pipeline runner (SSE) + paginated article feed + NER sidebar       │
│  Tab 2: UMAP 2D topic map (Plotly scatter, BERTopic keywords)               │
│  Tab 3: Contradiction explorer (PyVis network + side-by-side compare)       │
│  Tab 4: Topic frequency trends + sentiment ratio by source + summary card   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        SCHEDULED MAINTENANCE                                │
│                                                                             │
│  GitHub Actions cron (03:00 UTC daily)                                      │
│  └─► prefect_flow.py: ingestion_task → nlp_task                             │
│      (no LLM calls — preserves free-tier token budget)                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

ARTICLE LIFECYCLE — from RSS feed to dashboard

  INPUT: "Solar capacity doubles in Latin America" (Mongabay LATAM, ES)
  URL: https://es.mongabay.com/2024/06/solar-latam/

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  STEP 1 — feedparser + trafilatura                                       │
  │                                                                          │
  │  fetch_feed("mongabay_latam")   scrape_article(url, "mongabay_latam")    │
  │       │                                        │                         │
  │       ▼                                        ▼                         │
  │  url, feed_title,               url, title, text (full article body),    │
  │  feed_date, source              source, publication_date,                │
  │                                 ingestion_date (UTC),                    │
  │                                 sha256 = SHA-256(url.rstrip("/"))        │
  │                                 detected_language = None  ◄── not yet    │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                                             │  insert if sha256 not in RAW
                                             ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  MongoDB RAW                                                             │
  │                                                                          │
  │  {                                                                       │
  │    url:               "https://es.mongabay.com/2024/06/solar-latam/"     │
  │    title:             "La capacidad solar se duplica en América Latina"  │
  │    text:              "La energía solar en América Latina ha crecido..." │
  │    source:            "mongabay_latam"                                   │
  │    publication_date:  "2024-06-01"                                       │
  │    ingestion_date:    "2024-06-01T12:00:00+00:00"                        │
  │    sha256:            "a3f8c2..."   ◄── dedup key, unique index          │
  │    detected_language: null         ◄── filled in next step               │
  │  }                                                                       │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                                             │  url not in CLEAN → process
                                             ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  STEP 2 — langdetect + spaCy es_core_news_md                             │
  │                                                                          │
  │  detect(text[:2000]) → "es"    supported                                 |
  │       │                                                                  │
  │       ▼                                                                  │
  │  _clean_text()  →  strip HTML tags, collapse whitespace                  │
  │       │                                                                  │
  │       ▼                                                                  │
  │  nlp(clean_text)  →  spaCy Doc                                           │
  │    ├── tokens: [solar, capacidad, duplicar, América, Latina, energía...] │
  │    │   filter: is_alpha=True, is_stop=False, len>1                       │
  │    │   lemmatize → lemmatized_tokens: ["solar","capacidad","duplicar",   │
  │    │                                   "latina","energía","renovable"]   │
  │    └── ents: [(América Latina, LOC), (Brasil, GPE), (Chile, GPE)]        │
  │              → entities: [{"text":"América Latina","label":"LOC"}, ...]  │
  │                                                                          │
  │  _id from RAW removed  ◄── prevents duplicate key error on CLEAN index   │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                                             │  insert_clean_article()
                                             ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  MongoDB CLEAN                                                           │
  │                                                                          │
  │  {  ...all RAW fields (minus _id)...                                     │
  │    detected_language:  "es"                     ◄── overrides null       │
  │    lemmatized_tokens:  ["solar","capacidad","duplicar","energía",...]    │
  │    entities:           [{"text":"América Latina","label":"LOC"},...]     │
  │    ── embedding:  (not yet) ──────────────────────────────────────────── │
  │    ── topic_id:   (not yet) ──────────────────────────────────────────── │
  │  }                                                                       │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                                             │
                  ┌──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┐
                  │  STEP 3                  │  STEP 4                  │
                  ▼                          ▼                          │
  ┌───────────────────────────┐    ┌───────────────────────────┐        │
  │  HF Serverless API        │    │  BERTopic (joblib model)  │        │
  │                           │    │                           │        │
  │  input:                   │    │  assign_topics() loads    │        │
  │  "solar capacidad         │    │  bertopic_model.joblib    │        │
  │   duplicar energía..."    │    │                           │        │
  │  (lemmas joined)          │    │  UMAP: 384-dim → 5-dim    │        │
  │       │                   │    │  (cosine, n_neighbors=15) │        │
  │       ▼                   │---→│       │                   │        │
  │  paraphrase-multilingual  │    │  HDBSCAN: predict cluster │        │
  │  -MiniLM-L12-v2           │    │  (min_cluster_size=10)    │        │
  │       │                   │    │       │                   │        │
  │       ▼                   │    │       ▼                   │        │
  │  embedding: [0.12, -0.34, │    │  topic_id: 2              │        │
  │    0.08, ..., 0.21]       │    │  (topic 2 = renewable     │        │
  │  (384 floats, cosine sim) │    │   energy / solar)         │        │
  └───────────┬───────────────┘    └───────────┬───────────────┘        │
              │  $set {embedding}              │  $set {topic_id}       │
              └────────────────────────────────┘                        │
                                             │  update_one on CLEAN     │
                                             ▼                          │
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  MongoDB CLEAN  (enriched)                                           │
  │                                                                      │
  │  {  ...previous fields...                                            │
  │    embedding:  [0.12, -0.34, 0.08, ..., 0.21]  (384 floats)          │
  │    topic_id:   2                                                     │
  │  }                                                                   │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┘
                                             │  url not in CURATED + has topic_id
                                             ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  STEP 5 — Groq llama-3.1-8b-instant (json_mode=True)                     │
  │                                                                          │
  │  system: "You are a sentiment analysis engine...respond ONLY with JSON"  │
  │  user:   "Title: La capacidad solar...\n\nText: La energía solar en      │
  │           América Latina ha crecido... [first 1500 chars]"               │
  │                                                                          │
  │  response → {                                                            │
  │    "sentiment":          "positive",                                     │
  │    "intensity":          0.82,                                           │
  │    "principal_subject":  "solar energy Latin America",                   │
  │    "main_argument":      "Solar capacity doubled driven by policy..."    │
  │  }                                                                       │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                                             │  insert_curated_article()
                                             │  (_id from CLEAN stripped)
                                             ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  MongoDB CURATED  (final enriched schema)                                │
  │                                                                          │
  │  {                                                                       │
  │    url:               "https://es.mongabay.com/2024/06/solar-latam/"     │
  │    title:             "La capacidad solar se duplica en América Latina"  │
  │    text:              "La energía solar en América Latina ha crecido..." │
  │    source:            "mongabay_latam"                                   │
  │    detected_language: "es"                                               │
  │    publication_date:  "2024-06-01"                                       │
  │    ingestion_date:    "2024-06-01T12:00:00+00:00"                        │
  │    sha256:            "a3f8c2..."                                        │
  │    lemmatized_tokens: ["solar","capacidad","duplicar","energía",...]     │
  │    entities:          [{"text":"América Latina","label":"LOC"},...]      │
  │    embedding:         [0.12, -0.34, 0.08, ..., 0.21]  (384 floats)       │
  │    topic_id:          2                                                  │
  │    sentiment:         "positive"                      ◄── LLM output     │
  │    intensity:         0.82                            ◄── LLM output     │
  │    principal_subject: "solar energy Latin America"    ◄── LLM output     │
  │    main_argument:     "Solar capacity doubled..."     ◄── LLM output     │
  │  }                                                                       │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                                             │  read by LangGraph agents
                                             ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  STEP 6 — LangGraph agents (pymongo, synchronous)                        │
  │                                                                          │
  │  Analytical Agent:   aggregates this doc under source="mongabay_latam",  │
  │                       language="es", topic_id=2                          │
  │                                                                          │
  │  Contradiction Agent: Atlas Vector Search on CURATED embedding →         │
  │                        finds semantically similar articles with          │
  │                        sentiment="negative" (cosine sim ≥ 0.65)          │
  │                                                                          │
  │  Trend Agent:         counts this doc in ISO week for topic_id=2,        │
  │                        contributes to slope calculation                  │
  │                                                                          │
  │  Synthesis Agent:     doc's insights folded into narrative summary       │
  │                        → written to SUMMARIES collection                 │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                                             │
            ┌────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┐
            ▼                                ▼                            ▼
  GET /articles           GET /rag/search               GET /rag/topics/active
  (Tab 1 feed)            ?query="solar LATAM"          (Proyecto Agentes)
                          → this doc, score=0.93
                          (X-RAG-Key required)

### Key design decisions

**Why BERTopic over LDA for topic modeling:** LDA operates on bag-of-words — "solar" (EN) and "solaire" (FR) land in different topics because LDA sees tokens, not semantics. BERTopic operates on the 384-dimensional multilingual embeddings already stored in CLEAN: "solar energy" and "énergie solaire" are already close in that space because `paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2` was trained on parallel multilingual data. BERTopic inherits cross-lingual clustering for free.

**Why synchronous pymongo inside LangGraph agents and not motor:** LangGraph's `StateGraph.invoke()` is synchronous. Running `asyncio.run()` inside an already-running event loop (FastAPI) may raise problems. The agents use `pymongo` (blocking) while the FastAPI/pipeline layer uses `motor` (async). Both point to the same Atlas cluster via `MONGODB_URI`.

**Why Groq → Gemini fallback via OpenAI SDK:** Both Groq (`api.groq.com/openai/v1`) and Gemini (`generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/`) expose OpenAI-compatible endpoints. The same `openai.OpenAI` client handles both with only two string changes.

**Why train BERTopic once and `assign_topics()` on every run:** Retraining on every nightly run would renumber topics, breaking the dashboard's topic labels and the `/rag/topics/active` slope calculations. The model is trained once, serialized with `joblib` to `models/bertopic_model.joblib`, and loaded for inference on new articles.

**Why nightly maintenance runs only ingestion + NLP (not embeddings/sentiment/agents):** Ingestion (trafilatura + feedparser) and NLP (spaCy) are purely local. Embeddings require the HF Serverless API; sentiment requires Groq/Gemini (14,400 req/day combined). The split preserves free-tier budgets: by 06:00 UTC, new articles are in RAW and CLEAN, ready for the on-demand pipeline from the dashboard.

---

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.14+
- MongoDB Atlas account (M0 free tier, Paris region recommended)
- Hugging Face account (free token)
- Groq account (free API key — 14,400 req/day)
- Gemini account (free API key — 1,500 req/day fallback)

### 1. Clone and install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/JuanNicolasMendozaRoncancio/RAG-Multi-Agent-System.git
cd RAG-Multi-Agent-System

python -m venv .venv
# Windows (PowerShell)
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
# macOS/Linux
source .venv/bin/activate

pip install -r shared/requirements.txt
pip install -r nlp_worker/requirements.txt
pip install -r agent_worker/requirements.txt
pip install -r api/requirements.txt
pip install -r dashboard/requirements.txt

python -m spacy download es_core_news_md
python -m spacy download en_core_web_md
python -m spacy download fr_core_news_md
```

### 2. Configure environment

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env and fill in all values
```

```env
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster.mongodb.net/rag_climate
HF_TOKEN=hf_...
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
LLM_PROVIDER=groq
LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=ls__...       # optional — enables LangSmith tracing
LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true       # optional
LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=rag-climate   # optional
RAG_API_KEY=your-secret-key     # required for /rag/* endpoints
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000  # dashboard → API URL
```

### 3. Atlas Vector Search indexes

Create two vector search indexes in the Atlas UI (Search → Create Search Index → JSON Editor):

**On `clean` collection** — named `vector_index_1`:
```json
{
  "fields": [{
    "type": "vector",
    "path": "embedding",
    "numDimensions": 384,
    "similarity": "cosine"
  }]
}
```

**On `curated` collection** — named `vector_index`:
```json
{
  "fields": [{
    "type": "vector",
    "path": "embedding",
    "numDimensions": 384,
    "similarity": "cosine"
  }]
}
```

### 4. Run the API

```bash
# From project root, with .venv active
uvicorn api.main:app --port 8000 --reload
```

### 5. Run the dashboard

```bash
streamlit run dashboard/app.py
```

Open `http://localhost:8501` → Tab 1 → click **▶ Run pipeline**.

### 6. (Optional) Train BERTopic

If you have no pre-trained model yet (first run with enough articles):

```bash
python -c "
import asyncio
from dotenv import load_dotenv
load_dotenv()
from nlp_worker.topic_modeler import train_topic_model
asyncio.run(train_topic_model(min_articles=20))
"
```

The model is saved to `models/bertopic_model.joblib`.

### 7. (Optional) Docker Compose

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Services: `api` (8000), `dashboard` (8501), `nlp_worker`, `agent_worker`.

---

## API Reference

All endpoints are served by `uvicorn api.main:app --port 8000`.

### Pipeline

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `POST` | `/pipeline/run` | Trigger full pipeline — streams SSE events (6 steps) |
| `GET` | `/health` | MongoDB ping + LLM provider status |

**SSE event shape:**
```json
{"step": "NLP", "status": "done", "elapsed_s": 4.2, "processed": 12, "skipped": 0}
```
Steps: `Ingestion` → `NLP` → `Embeddings` → `BERTopic` → `Sentiment` → `Agents` → `COMPLETED`

### Data endpoints (internal — dashboard)

| Method | Endpoint | Key params | Source |
|--------|----------|------------|--------|
| `GET` | `/articles` | `source`, `language`, `sentiment`, `topic_id`, `limit`, `skip` | CURATED |
| `GET` | `/topics` | `days` | CURATED (aggregation) |
| `GET` | `/contradictions` | `days`, `threshold`, `max_pairs` | CURATED (Vector Search) |
| `GET` | `/trends` | `days` | CURATED (aggregation) |
| `GET` | `/summary` | — | SUMMARIES (latest) |
| `GET` | `/embeddings` | `limit` | CURATED (UMAP input) |

### Inter-system endpoints

Require `X-RAG-Key: <RAG_API_KEY>` header. Returns `422` if header absent, `401` if wrong.

| Method | Endpoint | Key params | Description |
|--------|----------|------------|-------------|
| `GET` | `/rag/search` | `query` (min 3 chars), `top_k` | Semantic search via Atlas Vector Search on CURATED |
| `GET` | `/rag/topics/active` | `days` | Rising topics ordered by linear regression slope |

---

### Authentication

The `/rag/*` endpoints use a simple shared-secret pattern via `X-RAG-Key` header. This is intentional — both systems run under the same infrastructure owner, so OAuth2/JWT would add complexity without a trust boundary benefit. The key is rotated via the `RAG_API_KEY` environment variable on both sides.

### `/rag/search` — semantic retrieval

```bash
curl "http://localhost:8000/rag/search?query=renewable+energy+transition&top_k=5" \
  -H "X-RAG-Key: your-secret-key"
```

```json
{
  "query": "renewable energy transition",
  "top_k": 5,
  "returned": 5,
  "results": [
    {
      "url": "https://...",
      "title": "Solar capacity doubles in Latin America",
      "source": "mongabay_latam",
      "detected_language": "es",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "intensity": 0.82,
      "topic_id": 2,
      "principal_subject": "solar energy Latin America",
      "main_argument": "Solar installations have doubled...",
      "publication_date": "2024-06-01",
      "extract": "La capacidad solar en América Latina...",
      "score": 0.9341
    }
  ]
}
```

**Why this response shape:** The RCA Agent needs `sentiment`, `intensity`, `topic_id`, and `main_argument` to contextualize electricity market anomalies with related climate policy coverage. `score` lets the agent threshold results by confidence. Full `text` and `embedding` are excluded to keep the payload lightweight.

### `/rag/topics/active` — rising topics

```bash
curl "http://localhost:8000/rag/topics/active?days=14" \
  -H "X-RAG-Key: your-secret-key"
```

```json
{
  "days": 14,
  "topics_count": 5,
  "topics": [
    {
      "topic_id": 3,
      "slope": 2.5,
      "total_articles": 18,
      "avg_intensity": 0.71,
      "dominant_sentiment": "negative",
      "weeks_observed": 2
    }
  ]
}
```

Topics are ordered by linear regression slope over weekly article counts — steepest growth first. The Narrative Agent uses this to enrich electricity market reports with "topics gaining momentum in climate discourse."

---

## Sentiment Benchmark

Three classifiers compared on the 222-article CURATED corpus:

| Classifier | Accuracy | F1-macro | Cohen's κ | N |
|-----------|----------|----------|-----------|---|
| LogisticRegression (5-fold CV on embeddings) | 0.7432 | 0.4793 | — | 222 |
| Groq `llama-3.1-8b-instant` vs CURATED labels | 0.9000 | 0.8360 | 0.7857 | 30 |
| Gemini `gemini-2.0-flash` vs CURATED labels | 0.9333 | 0.8333 | 0.8438 | 30 |

Groq/Gemini kappa > 0.60 (substantial agreement): the fallback mechanism does not degrade output quality. Full benchmark report: [`docs/sentiment_benchmark.md`](docs/sentiment_benchmark.md).

---

## LLM Strategy

```
chat_complete(messages, json_mode=False)
        │
        ▼
   LLM_PROVIDER env var
        │
  ┌─────┴──────┐
  │   groq     │   llama-3.1-8b-instant (primary)
  │            │   14,400 req/day free · sub-100ms TTFT
  └──────┬─────┘
  RateLimitError │ APITimeoutError (>30s) │ APIError
         ▼
  ┌─────────────┐
  │   gemini    │   gemini-2.0-flash (fallback)
  │             │   1,500 req/day free · OpenAI-compatible
  └─────────────┘
         │
   RuntimeError if both fail
```

Both providers are accessed via the OpenAI Python SDK pointed at their respective OpenAI-compatible base URLs. No provider-specific SDK is required. `LLM_PROVIDER=gemini` bypasses Groq entirely — useful for testing the fallback path.

---

## Tests

```bash
# Install dev dependencies
pip install pytest pytest-asyncio mongomock httpx python-dotenv

# Run all tests (no real API calls, no Atlas connection needed)
pytest tests/ -v

# Run specific test modules
pytest tests/test_embedder.py tests/test_pipeline.py -v
pytest tests/test_integration.py -v   # full pipeline chain (4 stages)
pytest tests/test_rag_endpoints.py -v  # auth + validation (FastAPI TestClient)
```

**Test architecture:** All external dependencies are mocked — MongoDB via `mongomock` wrapped in async-compatible `_AsyncCollection/_AsyncDb/_AsyncCursor` helpers (motor API contract, synchronous internals), HF API via `httpx.AsyncClient.post` patched with `AsyncMock`, LLMs via `chat_complete` patched. No real Atlas connection or API keys required for the unit and integration test suites.

**Key principle — patch where the name is looked up:**
```python
# WRONG: replaces the attribute in the source module,
# but embedder.py's local reference still points to the original
patch("shared.db.get_db", ...)

# CORRECT: patches the name in the namespace where it is used
patch("nlp_worker.embedder.get_db", ...)
```

### GitHub Actions

| Workflow | Trigger | What it runs |
|----------|---------|--------------|
| `tests.yml` | Push/PR to `master` | `test_integration.py` + `test_llm_client.py` (real API keys via secrets) |
| `nightly.yml` | Daily 03:00 UTC | `prefect_flow.py` — ingestion + NLP only (no LLM) |
| `agents_smoke.yml` | 1st & 15th of month | `run_agents(days=7)` — verifies full agent graph end-to-end |

---

## Infrastructure

Everything runs on free-tier services with zero cloud spend:

| Service | Purpose | Free tier used |
|---------|---------|----------------|
| MongoDB Atlas M0 | Primary database (4 collections, 2 Vector Search indexes) | 512 MB storage, Paris (AWS) |
| Hugging Face Serverless API | Multilingual embeddings (384-dim) | Rate-limited CPU inference |
| Groq Cloud | Primary LLM (`llama-3.1-8b-instant`) | 14,400 req/day |
| Google Gemini | Fallback LLM (`gemini-2.0-flash`) | 1,500 req/day |
| GitHub Actions | CI + nightly maintenance cron | 2,000 min/month |
| Prefect Cloud | Flow orchestration and monitoring | Free tier |
| Streamlit Community Cloud | Dashboard hosting | Free |
| Hugging Face Spaces | API hosting (CPU Basic) | Free |

